        "original_id": "869a6e72-5bf7-57e5-b6a7-81ac837bd9e0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Jackson, Bob Giraldi\n- Songs/Albums: “Beat It”, “Thriller”\n- Places/Studios: Westlake Recording Studios, Los Angeles\n- Roles: singer, director\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Jackson wrote and performed the song “Beat It,” which was released as a single from his sixth solo album “Thriller” in 1982.\n- Recording sessions for Michael Jackson’s album “Thriller” took place from April to November 1982 at Westlake Recording Studios in Los Angeles, and the production budget was $750,000.\n- Bob Giraldi was born on January 17, 1939, and he is an American film and television director.\n- Bob Giraldi is known for directing the film “Dinner Rush” and the music video for Michael Jackson’s song “Beat It”.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
